# Livewire 3 & Frontend Guidelines

## Component Structure
- Livewire class components live under `app/Livewire/` and blade views under `resources/views/livewire/`.
- Use PHP 8.4 typed properties and `#[Validate]` attributes for component validation.

## Performance & State
- Default to deferred or blurred binding (`wire:model.blur`) for standard text inputs unless instant reactive filtering is explicitly required (`wire:model.live`).
- Use Alpine.js (`x-data`, `x-show`, `x-cloak`, `x-transition`) for client-side interactions like dropdowns, modals, and tabs to minimize network roundtrips.
- Keep component payload light: pass IDs or lightweight DTOs/collections rather than deeply nested hydrated models when possible.

## Styling & Layout
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes exclusively. Avoid raw CSS or inline style tags.
- Ensure all interactive elements have accessible labels and distinct IDs.
- For chat or dynamic lists, ensure keying (`wire:key`) is applied to looped items.
